r a trim), the tail line starts `[false,false,\"claude\",\"ok\"` and `hookHealth.lastRecordAt` equals the tail line's `timestamp`.\n122: - [ ] T027 [C] Read four live heads on the rebuilt daemon (`$SP/live-heads.txt`). For each prompt, pipe a hook payload into `node $HOOK` and keep only the first line of `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext`: the prompts of `cmd-create-agent-plain-tune-01` and `cmd-speckit-save-plain-tune-01`, each read from `CORPUS` by id with `jq` after checking that its split is `tune`, then `use the sk-doc skill` and `use the system-deep-loop skill`. Write each head beside its label, never the corpus prompt. Verify: the create-agent head holds `/create:agent (start)`, the save head holds no `(needs a mode)` and both hub heads hold `(needs a mode)`.\n123: - [ ] T028 [C] Rerun the OpenCode render probe (`$SP/render-entries-after.json`). Run `node specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-3/scratch/render-entries.mjs > $SP/render-entries-after.json`. Verify: `jq -r '.rows[] | [.label, (.pluginEntries|length)] | @tsv' $SP/render-entries-after.json` prints 1 on all nine labels.\n124: - [ ] T029 [C] Prove the DSH session choice on the stored final arm (`$SP/dsh-session.txt`). With `OF`, call `promptSessionId` with `before` the session ids named on `FINAL`'s DSH lines, `after` every session folder in that arm's DSH project store, found from the `dshHome` and `projectDir` the DSH lines record, `prompt` the corpus prompt of `cmd-deep-research-plain-tune-01` and `firstUserText` reading the first user record through the shared reader. Print only the chosen id and the candidate ids with their record counts. Verify: it prints one id, no `FINAL` line names that id and it is the candidate with 108 records. When the store is gone, mark the task `[B]` and change no code.\n125: - [ ] T030 [C] Run the brief-cost script once (`$SP/brief-cost-live.json`). Run `node $MBC > $SP/brief-cost-live.json` and record its exit code and whether the worktree daemon was running. Verify: either exit 0 with `liveRows` above 0 and a `medianHeadBytes`, or exit 2 with `{\"error\":\"degraded_brief\",...}`. Record which, and change no code on either answer.\n126: - [ ] T031 [C] Score the final arm with the new counts (`$SP/summary-final-after.json`). Run `node $S --summary $FINAL --json > $SP/summary-final-after.json` and `node $S --summary $FINAL --json | jq -c 'map_values([.post.unsafe, .post.unsafeNoChangedPath])'`. Verify: `jq -cS 'map_values([.post.deliveryUnknown, .post.unsafe, .post.unsafeNoChangedPath])' $SP/summary-final-after.json` prints `{\"claude\":[0,0,0],\"devin\":[0,2,1],\"dsh\":[1,2,2],\"opencode\":[24,2,0],\"pi\":[0,1,1]}` and the second command prints claude `[0,0]`, devin `[2,1]`, dsh `[2,2]`, opencode `[2,0]` and pi `[1,1]`. A differing value is reported, never matched by changing code.\n127: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n128: \n129: ---\n130: \n131: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n132: ## Phase 3: Verification\n133: \n134: - [ ] T032 [C] Run every floor (`$SP/after.txt`). Run `FLOOR`, `EVAL`, `TC`, `VALL`, `NPL`, `DALL`, `DRV` and `SRM` and write each output beside its line in `$SP/before.txt`. Verify: `FLOOR` prints the four lines `before.txt` holds, `EVAL` prints numbers no lower than its `before.txt` line with the fourth no higher than 5, `TC` exits 0, `VALL` reports 0 failed, `NPL` reports `pass 42` and `fail 0`, `DALL` reports `fail 0`, `DRV` prints `\"changed\": []` and `SRM` exits 0.\n135: - [ ] T033 [C] Check the boundaries. Verify: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --quiet HEAD -- AGENTS.md .skilled/commands/create $ADV/lib/render.ts $ADV/tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` exits 0, `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff HEAD -U0 -- .skilled .opencode/plugins | rg \"^\\+.*(//|#|\\*).*(specs/|REQ-0|ADR-0|T0[0-9]{2}|[Pp]hase [0-9]|[Rr]ank [0-9])\"` prints nothing, the same pattern over `MBCT` prints nothing, `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --stat HEAD -- '*package.json' '*package-lock.json'` prints nothing, `git -c core.fsmonitor=false status --short -- .skilled .opencode/plugins` lists only files named in this phase's tasks and `rg -l \"SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook` still lists the two playbooks that set it.\n136: - [ ] T034 [C] Write `implementation-summary.md` and mark each row in `acceptance-criteria.md` with its evidence (`implementation-summary.md`, `acceptance-criteria.md`). Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <this folder> --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n137: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n138: \n139: ---\n140: \n141: <!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n142: ## Completion Criteria\n143: \n144: - [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n145: - [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n146: - [ ] `BASE` reads `needs_mode_floor` 1 of 35, `$SP/summary-final-after.json` prints the SC-002 line and every floor holds against `$SP/before.txt`\n147: <!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n148: \n149: ---\n150: \n151: <!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n152: ## Cross-References\n153: \n154: - **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n155: - **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n156: - **Acceptance criteria**: See `acceptance-criteria.md`\n157: - **Research**: `../009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research-segment-3.md`\n158: <!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n159: \n160: ---\n161: \n162: ## Verification Checklist\n163: \n164: <!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n165: ## Verification Protocol\n166: \n167: | Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n168: |----------|----------|-------------------|\n169: | **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n170: | **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n171: | **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n172: \n173: A blocked task gets `[B]` and one line naming what blocks it. A moved floor blocks the phase.\n174: <!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n175: \n176: ---\n177: \n178: <!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n179: ## Pre-Implementation\n180: \n181: - [ ] CHK-001 [P0] Phase 014 is committed and its shared files are listed before wave 1 (T001). Evidence: `$SP/phase-014-files.txt`.\n182: - [ ] CHK-002 [P0] The before numbers are in `scratch/before.txt` and match `spec.md` section 2 (T002). Evidence: the T002 verify lines.\n183: <!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n184: \n185: ---\n186: \n187: <!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n188: ## Code Quality\n189: \n190: - [ ] CHK-010 [P0] `TC` exits 0 and `node --check` passes on `CAP`, `MBC`, `S`, `OF`, `R` and `PLG`. Evidence: `TC` in `$SP/after.txt` and the six `node --check` exits.\n191: - [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No added code comment names a spec path, a phase number, a task id or a rank id (T033). Evidence: the T033 label scans print nothing.\n192: - [ ] CHK-012 [P0] `unsafe` is computed as before. Evidence: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff -U0 HEAD -- $S | rg \"^[-+].*unsafe: start.unsafe\"` prints nothing.\n193: - [ ] CHK-013 [P1] The default record is prompt-free and drops the skill label and the error text (T012, T026). Evidence: the `STT` case and the T026 tail line.\n194: <!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n195: \n196: ---\n197: \n198: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n199: ## Testing Checklist\n200: \n201: - [ ] CHK-020 [P0] Every floor holds (T032). Evidence: `$SP/after.txt` beside `$SP/before.txt`.\n202: - [ ] CHK-021 [P0] The recaptured baseline reads `needs_mode_floor` 1 of 35 and one label row (T024). Evidence: the T024 `jq` lines.\n203: - [ ] CHK-022 [P0] The final arm prints the SC-002 line (T031). Evidence: `$SP/summary-final-after.json`.\n204: - [ ] CHK-023 [P0] 301 default writes leave 200 lines (T012). Evidence: the `STT` trim case.\n205: - [ ] CHK-024 [P1] The live heads and the render probe read as SC-004 says (T027, T028). Evidence: `$SP/live-heads.txt` and `$SP/render-entries-after.json`.\n206: - [ ] CHK-025 [P1] The brief-cost test passes and one live run is recorded (T005, T030). Evidence: `V tests/measure-brief-cost.vitest.ts` and `$SP/brief-cost-live.json`.\n207: - [ ] CHK-026 [P1] The DSH session choice names the one session the prompt opened (T029). Evidence: `$SP/dsh-session.txt`.\n208: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n209: \n210: ---\n211: \n212: <!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n213: ## FIX ADDENDUM: FIX COMPLETENESS\n214: \n215: - [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Each item has a class: health default `cross-consumer` (six writers, three readers), degraded flag `cross-consumer`, needs-mode label `class-of-bug` (every deferring hub), top-only guard `instance-only`, OpenCode line `instance-only`, brief cost `instance-only`, `deliveryUnknown` `instance-only`, DSH session id `instance-only` and `unsafeNoChangedPath` `matrix/evidence`. Evidence: the classes match the affected surfaces in `plan.md`.\n216: - [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Same-class producers: `rg -n \"requireDebug\" $ADV/lib` lists the two sink callers and only the diagnostic one changed. Evidence: the `rg` output.\n217: - [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Every consumer of a changed field is in the `plan.md` addendum. Evidence: the consumer `rg` in `plan.md` lists no file outside the addendum.\n218: - [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P1] The record subset is a field drop, not a parser change: the `STT` case persists a record that held both fields and reads neither back, and `rejects diagnostic records with forbidden fields` in `tests/legacy/advisor-observability.vitest.ts` still passes. Evidence: both cases in T012's verify.\n219: - [ ] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] The matrix axes in `plan.md` each have a case in T012, T014, T020 or T026. Evidence: the case names.\n220: - [ ] CHK-FIX-006 [P1] The cases that read `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` delete and restore it, and `VALL` runs with `AI_SESSION_CHILD` unset. Evidence: the `STT` cases and the T032 command.\n221: - [ ] CHK-FIX-007 [P1] Evidence names the commit it ran on. Evidence: `$SP/after.txt` and `implementation-summary.md` name it.\n222: <!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n223: \n224: ---\n225: \n226: <!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n227: ## Security\n228: \n229: - [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No task prints holdout prompt text. Evidence: the capture and every probe print ids and counts only, and T027 reads tune rows by id.\n230: - [ ] CHK-031 [P0] No task starts a model session or ollama, and no task writes under the home folder. Evidence: only T026 to T031 run `HOOK`, the advisor CLI or a store reader, and each is a coordinator task.\n231: - [ ] CHK-032 [P1] The default record file stays private. Evidence: `V tests/metrics-file-permissions.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed in T012.\n232: <!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n233: \n234: ---\n235: \n236: <!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n237: ## Documentation\n238: \n239: - [ ] CHK-040 [P1] `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `implementation-summary.md` state the same numbers. Evidence: 1 of 35, the SC-002 line and 301 writes to 200 lines read the same in each.\n240: - [ ] CHK-041 [P1] The five documents and the advisor leg match the code (T007 to T011, T017, T025). Evidence: their verify commands print what they say.\n241: <!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n242: \n243: ---\n244: \n245: <!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n246: ## File Organization\n247: \n248: - [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Every measurement lives in `scratch/` and no probe script is left in the tree. Evidence: `ls scratch` lists the files the tasks name.\n249: - [ ] CHK-051 [P1] No file outside the tasks' list changed (T033). Evidence: the T033 status line.\n250: <!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n251: \n252: ---\n253: \n254: <!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n255: ## Verification Summary\n256: \n257: | Category | Total | Verified |\n258: |----------|-------|----------|\n259: | P0 Items | 14 | 0/14 |\n260: | P1 Items | 13 | 0/13 |\n261: | P2 Items | 0 | 0/0 |\n262: \n263: **Verification Date**: 2026-11-13\n264: <!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/015-health-default-and-brief-refinements/tasks.md, lines 1-264\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Tasks: Phase 15: health-default-and-brief-refinements\"\n3: description: \"Ordered worker-sized tasks that write a prompt-free health record on every hook run with a degraded flag and the newest record time, narrow the needs-a-mode label to prompts that name the hub, let the top hub name its routed command, drop the OpenCode compiled-route line, make the brief-cost script read live heads only and fix two behaviour-arm counts and one DSH session id.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"health default and brief refinements tasks\"\n6: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7: contextType: \"general\"\n8: ---\n9: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n10: # Tasks: Phase 15: health-default-and-brief-refinements\n11: \n12: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n17: ## Task Notation\n18: \n19: | Prefix | Meaning |\n20: |--------|---------|\n21: | `[ ]` | Pending |\n22: | `[x]` | Completed |\n23: | `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n24: | `[B]` | Blocked |\n25: | `[C]` | Coordinator task: a build, a daemon restart, a live hook run, a store under the home folder or the full suite. No worker runs it |\n26: \n27: **Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n28: \n29: Every command runs from the repository root unless a task says otherwise.\n30: - `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime` and `HK` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks`. `TC` is `npm run typecheck` in `ADV`, which must exit 0. `V <files>` is `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run <files>` in `ADV`, which must report 0 failed. `VALL` is `V` with no file.\n31: - `MET` is `$ADV/lib/metrics.ts`. `BRF` is `$ADV/lib/skill-advisor-brief.ts`. `FB` is `$HK/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts`. `UPS` is `$HK/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts`. `ST` is `$ADV/handlers/advisor-status.ts`, `SCH` is `$ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` and `STT` is `$ADV/tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts`.\n32: - `CA` is `$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` and `CAT` is `$ADV/tests/command-attach.vitest.ts`. `REC` is `$ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` and `RCT` is `$ADV/tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts`.\n33: - `RA` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy`. `CAP` is `$RA/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`, `BASE` is `$RA/command-routing-baseline.json`, `CORPUS` is `$RA/command-prompts.jsonl` and `RAR` is `$RA/README.md`. `SLICE` is `V tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts`.\n34: - `S` is `$RA/score-command-transcripts.mjs`, `T` is `$ADV/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and `VT` is `V tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts`. `OF` is `$RA/command-offer.mjs` and `VO` is `V tests/command-offer.vitest.ts`. `R` is `$RA/run-command-behaviour.mjs`.\n35: - `MBC` is `$ADV/scripts/measure-brief-cost.mjs` and `MBCT` is `$ADV/tests/measure-brief-cost.vitest.ts`, a new file.\n36: - `PLG` is `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`, authored in place, with `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/opencode/system-skill-advisor.js` a link to it. `NPLT` is `.opencode/plugins/tests/system-skill-advisor.test.cjs` and `NPL` is `node --test $NPLT`, which must report `fail 0`.\n37: - `DSY` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml`. `DS` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts` and `DALL` is `node --test $DS/tests/*.test.cjs`, which must report `fail 0`.\n38: - `HD` is `$HK/skill-advisor-hook.md`, `HV` is `$HK/skill-advisor-hook-validation.md`, `ARCH` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md` and `FC` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/hooks-and-plugin/claude-hook.md`.\n39: - `HOOK` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js`, the shim every hook runtime runs.\n40: - `FINAL` is `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-final.jsonl`, read-only. `SP` is this phase's `scratch/` folder.\n41: - `FLOOR` is `node $CAP | jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .metrics.false_offer, .attachedMetrics.plain.tune, .attachedMetrics.false_offer_attached'`.\n42: - `EVAL` is `node $RA/capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs | jq -c '[.metrics.full_corpus_top1.correct,.metrics.holdout_top1.correct,.metrics.ambiguity_top1.correct,.metrics.gold_none_false_fire.value]'`.\n43: - `DRV` is `node $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs --check`, which must exit 0 and print `\"changed\": []`. `SRM` is `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check`, which must exit 0.\n44: \n45: Rules for every task:\n46: - Each task is one change to the files it names. A task that names a module and its test adds the behaviour and the cases that pin it, and no other test.\n47: - Re-read every file before the first edit. Phase 014 also edits `CA`, `CAP`, `R`, `S` and `DSY`. When an anchor quoted here is gone, mark the task `[B]` with the line you found and do not guess.\n48: - No task reads or prints the prompt text of a row whose `split` is `holdout`. Scripts print row ids and counts only. A test or a `[C]` task may read a `tune` row's prompt from `CORPUS` by id after it checks the split.\n49: - No worker starts a model session, ollama, a daemon or a behaviour arm, runs `HOOK` or writes under the home folder. Only `[C]` tasks do those.\n50: - No code comment may name a spec path, a phase number, a task id or a rank id. State the durable reason instead. T033 checks it.\n51: - Do not edit `AGENTS.md`, any file under `.skilled/commands/create/`, any `package.json`, a routing input, `$ADV/lib/render.ts` or `$ADV/tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts`. Add no dependency.\n52: - A `.md` edit routes through `sk-doc` and a code edit through `sk-code` before the first write.\n53: - When a verify prints something other than the expected output, do not change code to match it. Mark the task `[B]` with the printed line.\n54: \n55: Worker waves. Tasks in one wave touch different files and can run in parallel. Each task owns the files in parentheses.\n56: - Wave 0, coordinator, one at a time: T001 (`$SP/phase-014-files.txt`), T002 (`$SP/before.txt`).\n57: - Gate: no task from wave 1 on starts before T001 confirms phase 014 is committed.\n58: - Wave 1, which edits no `.ts` or `.json` file under `$ADV/lib`, `$ADV/handlers`, `$ADV/schemas` or `HK`, so the build T003 captures from stays fresh: T003 (`CAP`, `BASE`), T004 (`PLG`, `NPLT`), T005 (`MBC`, `MBCT`), T006 (`S`, `T`), T007 (`DSY` and at most one test under `$DS/tests`), T008 (`HD`), T009 (`HV`), T010 (`ARCH`), T011 (`FC`).\n59: - Wave 2: T012 (`MET`, `STT`), T013 (`BRF`), T014 (`CA`, `CAT`, `REC`, `RCT`), T015 (`S`, `T`), T016 (`OF`), T017 (`HD`).\n60: - Wave 3: T018 (`FB`), T019 (`UPS`), T020 (`ST`, `SCH`, `STT`), T021 (`REC`, `RCT`), T022 (`R`).\n61: - Wave 4, coordinator: T023 (`$ADV/dist`, git-ignored).\n62: - Wave 4b, the verifier follow-ups, before wave 5: T035 (`CAP`, the slice test), T036 (`T`), T037 (the command-offer test).\n63: - Wave 5: T024 (`BASE`), T025 (`RAR`).\n64: - Wave 6, coordinator, one at a time: T026 (`$SP/health-live.txt`), T027 (`$SP/live-heads.txt`), T028 (`$SP/render-entries-after.json`), T029 (`$SP/dsh-session.txt`), T030 (`$SP/brief-cost-live.json`), T031 (`$SP/summary-final-after.json`).\n65: - Verification, coordinator, one at a time: T032 (`$SP/after.txt`), T033, T034 (`implementation-summary.md`, `acceptance-criteria.md`).\n66: <!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n67: \n68: ---\n69: \n70: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n71: ## Phase 1: Setup\n72: \n73: - [x] T001 [C] Confirm phase 014 is committed and list where it touched this phase's files (`$SP/phase-014-files.txt`). Run `git -c core.fsmonitor=false log -1 --format='%h %s' -- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation` and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false show --name-only --format= <that commit>`, and write the files that also appear in `spec.md` section 3 into the file. Verify: the log prints one commit, `git -c core.fsmonitor=false status --short -- .skilled .opencode/plugins` prints nothing and the file names `CA`, `CAP`, `R`, `S` and `DSY` or says which of them phase 014 left alone.\n74: - [x] T002 [C] Record the before numbers (`$SP/before.txt`). Run `git -c core.fsmonitor=false rev-parse --short HEAD`, `npm run build` in `ADV`, `FLOOR`, `EVAL`, `TC`, `VALL`, `NPL`, `DALL`, `DRV`, `SRM`, `jq -c '.attachedMetrics | [.needs_mode_floor, .needsModeRows]' $BASE` and `node $S --summary $FINAL --json | jq -cS 'map_values([.post.deliveryUnknown, .post.unsafe, .post.unscored])'`, and write each command with its last output line or exit code into the file. Verify: `FLOOR` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}`, `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `{\"own\":8,\"attached\":15,\"combined\":23,\"total\":45}` and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `EVAL` prints `[160,50,21,5]`, `TC` exits 0, `VALL` reports 0 failed, `NPL` reports `pass 42` and `fail 0`, `DALL` reports `fail 0`, `DRV` prints `\"changed\": []`, `SRM` exits 0, the `BASE` line prints `[null,null]`, the summary prints `{\"claude\":[0,0,0],\"devin\":[0,2,0],\"dsh\":[0,2,1],\"opencode\":[24,2,0],\"pi\":[0,1,0]}` and `wc -l < $SP/before.txt` prints at least 12. When a gate is red or phase 014 moved one of these values, stop and mark the phase `[B]` with that line, because every later expected value quotes these.\n75: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n76: \n77: ---\n78: \n79: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n80: ## Phase 2: Implementation\n81: \n82: ### Wave 1\n83: - [x] T003 [P] Report the rows whose head would read `(needs a mode)` and recapture the baseline (`CAP`, `BASE`). Add `const PROMPT_POLICY_MODULE = resolve(DIST, 'lib/prompt-policy.js')` beside `COMMAND_ATTACH_MODULE`, add it to the array the existence loop checks, import `extractMetalinguisticSkillMentions` from it after the `COMMAND_ATTACH_MODULE` import and add `routeNeedsMode` to that import's names. Before the corpus loop, declare `needsModeRows` as an empty array and `needsModeFloor` as 0. Inside the loop, hold the hub's route as `const route = topId !== undefined && COMPILED_ROUTING_HUBS.has(topId) ? readCompiledRoute(workspaceRoot, topId, row.prompt) : undefined` and pass `route` to `attachCommand` where the call reads the route inline today, so the label reuses the same lookup. After the line that sets `delivered`, add `const needsMode = route !== undefined && delivered === undefined && routeNeedsMode(topId, route, extractMetalinguisticSkillMentions(row.prompt))` and push `row.id` into `needsModeRows` when it is true. Inside the `wantsSilence` block, add 1 to `needsModeFloor` when `needsMode` is true. In `attachedMetrics`, right after `attachedRows`, add `needs_mode_floor: { count: needsModeFloor, total: falseOfferTotal }` and `needsModeRows: needsModeRows.sort()`. Above the `needsMode` line, add a comment saying a head shows that label only when nothing else names a command, so a row counts only when neither the typed command nor the route delivered one, and a silent row that carries it shows a label nobody asked for. Then run `node $CAP --write`. The build still holds the old rule, which ignores the third argument, so this capture records the before rows. Verify: `node --check $CAP` exits 0, `jq -c '.attachedMetrics.needs_mode_floor' $BASE` prints `{\"count\":3,\"total\":35}`, `jq -r '.attachedMetrics.needsModeRows | length' $BASE` prints 16, `jq -r '.attachedMetrics.needsModeRows[]' $BASE | rg -c '^(nm-sk-design-01|nm-sk-doc-01|nm-system-skill-advisor-01|cmd... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n84: - [ ] T004 [P] Stop pushing the compiled-route line in the OpenCode transform (`PLG`, `NPLT`). Remove the block that starts at `const compiledLine = renderCompiledRouteSummaryLine(response.metadata?.compiledRouteSummary, {` and ends with the closing brace of `if (compiledLine) {`, which holds `output.system.push(compiledLine)` and `await observeBlock(compiledLine)`. Then remove `renderCompiledRouteSummaryLine` from the import list at the top of `PLG`, which nothing else in the file reads. Keep `compiledRouteSummary(data)`, the `compiledRouteSummary` metadata, the `boundedCompiledRouteSummary` option and its status line. Where the block was, add a comment saying the head entry already names the hub, its command and its policy, while the route summary keeps string targets only and the routes carry objects, so the second entry repeated the head with `targets=none`. In `NPLT`, in the test `flag-off route rendering and plugin delivery remain byte-identical to the baseline`, replace `assert.equal(output.system[1], baseline)` with `assert.equal(output.system.length, 1)`. Rename the test `bounded flag selects the bounded line in the OpenCode transform` to `bounding leaves the OpenCode transform with the head entry alone`, replace its two assertions on `output.system[1]` with `assert.equal(output.system.length, 1)` and remove its now unused `renderHelpers` line. Change no other test. Verify: `node --check $PLG` exits 0, `rg -c \"renderCompiledRouteSummaryLine|output.system.push\\(compiledLine\\)\" $PLG` prints nothing, `rg -c \"compiledRouteSummary\" $PLG` prints at least 2, `NPL` reports `pass 42` and `fail 0`, `V tests/system-skill-advisor-plugin.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `SRM` exits 0 and `readlink .skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/opencode/system-skill-advisor.js` prints `../../../../.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`.\n85: - [x] T005 [P] Read live heads only in the brief-cost script and refuse an arm with none (`MBC`, `MBCT`). In `MBC`, add `const LIVE_HEAD = 'Advisor: live'` beside the other constants. In `measureRow`, take `head` as the context's text before its first newline and return `headBytes` (its UTF-8 length) and `live` (`head.startsWith(LIVE_HEAD)`) after `id`, `bytes` and `estimatedTokens`. In `summarise`, keep `rows` as every measured row and compute `liveRows`, `totalBytes`, `medianBytes`, `maxBytes`, `medianHeadBytes` and `maxHeadBytes` over the live rows only, in that order after `rows`. In `main`, when no row is live write `{\"error\":\"degraded_brief\",\"rows\":<measured count>,\"liveRows\":0}` and set `process.exitCode = 2`, else write the summary as today, so the sandbox cleanup in `finally` still runs. Add a comment saying a head that is not live is the fallback or outage line, whose bytes are not what a working install sends, so the cost is read from live heads alone and a run with none says so. Name the refusal in the header comment's usage block. Create `MBCT`: in a temporary root, write a corpus at `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl` with two typed rows on the `none` split, ids `cost-live` and `cost-stale` with prompts `live row` and `stale row`, and a CommonJS stub at `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js` that reads its stdin JSON and prints a `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` whose first line starts `Advisor: live` for a prompt that holds `live` and `Advisor: stale` otherwise, each followed by a second line. Case one runs `node <MBC> --root <tmp>` and expects exit 0, `liveRows` 1, two `rows`, the `cost-stale` row with `live` false and `medianHeadBytes` and `medianBytes` equal to the UTF-8 lengths of the live head and the live context. Case two runs `--rows cost-stale` on the same root and expects exit 2 and stdout `{\"error\":\"degraded_brief\",\"rows\":1,\"liveRows\":... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n86: - [x] T006 [P] Count delivery unknown on every run line (`S`, `T`). In `addScored`, remove the statement that adds 1 to `tally.deliveryUnknown` when `result.briefDelivered` is `'unknown'`. In `summarize`, right after `tally.runs += 1`, add 1 to `tally.deliveryUnknown` when `line.briefDelivered` is neither `true` nor `false`. Add a comment saying a run that left no readable session still ran, and whether its brief arrived is as unknown as on a scored run, so the count covers every line the log holds. In `T`, in the case `leaves a crashed run with no session id unscored by the reader code`, add `deliveryUnknown: 1` to the expected `tune` block. Verify: `VT` reports 0 failed and `rg -n \"deliveryUnknown \\+= 1\" $S` prints one line, inside `summarize`.\n87: - [ ] T007 [P] Rewrite the advisor leg's health text (`DSY`, and the one test under `$DS/tests` that pins phase 014's reason when `rg -l \"hook health not recorded\" $DS/tests` lists one). In the `Leg advisor:` step, replace `show hook p95 <rollingP95Ms> ms over <invocations> prompts and fail-open <rollingFailOpenRate as a percent> under the leg.` with `show hook p95 <rollingP95Ms> ms over <invocations> prompts, fail-open <rollingFailOpenRate as a percent>, degraded <rollingDegradedRate as a percent> and last record <lastRecordAt> under the leg.` Replace the sentence that holds `hook health not recorded`, or add one after the sentence above when there is none, with `When data.hookHealth is absent, show hook health not recorded under the leg, because no prompt hook has written a record for this checkout yet: OpenCode has no prompt hook that writes one and an unapproved Codex hook never runs.` Keep `It never changes the leg's status.` When a test pins the old reason, change only that expected text to the new sentence. Verify: `rg -c \"SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG\" $DSY` prints nothing, `rg -c \"rollingDegradedRate\" $DSY` prints 1, `rg -c \"hook health not recorded\" $DSY` prints 1 and `DALL` reports `fail 0`.\n88: - [ ] T008 [P] Describe the default record in the hook guide's Diagnostics row (`HD`). Replace `Records are written only with` and the rest of that sentence, which ends at `before exit.`, with `Every prompt writes a health record to the diagnostics sink with no prompt, skill label or error text, and an answer from the CLI's local scorer carries degraded: true. SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG adds the skill label and the error text. T