carries degraded: true.`, keeping both names in backticks. Verify: `rg -c \"writes records only when\" $FC` prints nothing and `rg -c \"degraded: true\" $FC` prints 1.\n92: \n93: ### Wave 2\n94: - [x] T012 [P] Write a health record by default and report its degraded share and age (`MET`, `STT`). In `AdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord`, add `readonly degraded?: boolean`. In `createAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord`, add `readonly degraded?: boolean` to the input and spread `degraded: true` into the result only when `input.degraded === true`. In `validateAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord`, also require `record.degraded` to be `undefined` or a boolean. In `persistAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord`, serialize the record as it is when `process.env.SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` is set and otherwise a copy without `skillLabel` and `errorDetails`, and pass `{ requireDebug: false }` to `writeBoundedJsonl` in both cases. Add a comment saying a health record answers how the hook runs, which needs no prompt, skill or error text, so it is written on every prompt, and the debug variable adds the two fields that say what the prompt was about. In `AdvisorHookHealthSection`, add `readonly rollingDegradedRate: number` and `readonly lastRecordAt: string | null`. In `buildAdvisorHookHealthSection`, set `rollingDegradedRate` to the share of `lastInvocations` whose `degraded` is true (0 when there are none) and `lastRecordAt` to the `timestamp` of the last element of `lastInvocations`, or `null` when it is empty. In `STT`, add two cases after `reports hook health from durable diagnostic records`, each deleting `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` and restoring it afterwards. `writes a health record without the debug variable and keeps the skill label out` persists one record built with `skillLabel: 'sk-doc'`, `errorDetails: 'probe detail'` and `degraded: true`, reads the one line at `advisorHookDiagnosticsPath(root)` and expects no `skillLabel`, no `errorDetails`, `degraded` true and `readAdvisorStatus({ workspaceRoot: root }).hookHeal