{"type":"text","timestamp":1794565932530,"sessionID":"ses_e2b8c79c0ffeLCVolj1hMkPIuC","part":{"id":"prt_1d476f073001RHR3m2tCaW6sjf","sessionID":"ses_e2b8c79c0ffeLCVolj1hMkPIuC","messageID":"msg_1d476c887001UXLEVM12JI2wIO","type":"text","text":"T035 is done. The needs-a-mode row list now excludes holdout ids, and the slice test asserts it.\n\n**Files written**\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`: changed `if (needsMode) needsModeRows.push(row.id);` to `if (needsMode && publishRow) needsModeRows.push(row.id);` and added the two-line comment explaining that the list names rows with their outcome, so a holdout row stays out as it stays out of the row maps.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts`: added `readonly needsModeRows?: readonly string[]` to the local `attached` type and `...(attached.needsModeRows ?? [])` to the array the `published` set is built from.\n\n**Test-first evidence (OBSERVED)**\n`env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` in `ADV` failed the new assertion with `AssertionError: the baseline publishes a per-row outcome for 8 holdout ids: expected [ …(8) ] to deeply equal []`, exactly the 8 ids the task predicted. A second case, `matches the captured totals`, also failed against the committed baseline because phase 014's label rule is live while `BASE` still holds the old capture. That drift is what T024 recaptures, so I did not touch it.\n\n**Verify output (OBSERVED)**\n```\n$ node --check .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs\nnode-check-exit=0\n\n$ node .skilled/.../capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs | jq -c '[.attachedMetrics.needsModeRows[] | select(test(\"holdout\"))] | length'\n0\ncapture-exit=0\n\n$ rg -c \"needsMode && publishRow\" .skilled/.../capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs\n1\n```\nNo `--write` was run. `command-routing-baseline.json` still reads `{\"count\":3,\"total\":35}` with 16 `needsModeRows`, the values T003 recorded, so the plain capture left it untouched.\n\n**Not done**\n`SLICE` is not green yet: the `publishes no holdout row` case compares against the committed baseline, which still lists 8 holdout ids until T024 recaptures `BASE`. T035's own verify commands all pass.\n\nSKILL ROUTING: sk-code → sk-code-skilled (compiled route, single target)\nARTIFACT: sk-code-skilled → javascript style guide, shared naming and commenting, TypeScript surface rules\nREPO RULES: prevent-overengineering.md, evidence-and-proof.md, communication.md, communication-handoff.md\n\nNothing is blocked on you. T024 recaptures the baseline and turns the slice case green.","time":{"start":1794565927027,"end":1794565932530}}}
